    63	/**
    64	 * The owner of the IOU report is the account who is owed money and the manager is the one who owes money!
    65	 * In case the owner/manager swap, we need to update the owner of the IOU report and the report total, since it is always positive.
    66	 * For example: if user1 owes user2 $10, then we have: {ownerAccountID: user2, managerID: user1, total: $10 (a positive amount, owed to user2)}
    67	 * If user1 requests $17 from user2, then we have: {ownerAccountID: user1, managerID: user2, total: $7 (still a positive amount, but now owed to user1)}
    68	 *
    69	 * @param isDeleting - whether the user is deleting the expense
    70	 * @param isUpdating - whether the user is updating the expense
    71	 */
